# Agent orchestration

The main chat **orchestrates**. Specialists do the lane work.

## Every user message

Before doing the work, put this block at the top of your reply (even when no specialist is needed):

```markdown
**Agents:** `name` (why) → `name` (why)
```

If the main chat will do it alone: `**Agents:** main chat only — <one-line why>`.

Then **launch** the first required specialist(s) with Task in that same turn. Do not only describe them.

## How to launch

Task parameters:

- `subagent_type`: `product-manager` | `ui-ux-designer` | `software-architect` | `dba` | `ai-expert` | `qa-engineer` | `devops` | `executor` | `planner`
- `model`: `gpt-5.6-sol-medium` (PM, UX, architect, DBA, AI expert, planner) or `gemini-3.7-flash-high` (executor, QA, DevOps)
- Never `inherit`. Never Grok / Composer / Claude unless the user named that listed model
- `run_in_background: false` unless two specialists are independent (then launch both in one turn)
- Prompt must include the user request, FitTrack context, and what that agent should return

Follow each agent's **Handoff** footer. If they name a Next agent and did not already launch it, you launch it next with their Brief.

Handoff table: `.cursor/agents/HANDOFF.md`.

## Pick the first agent

| Request | First |
| --- | --- |
| What to build, roadmap, prioritize, expand features | `product-manager` |
| Layout, copy, flows, theme | `ui-ux-designer` |
| Architecture, auth, where code lives | `software-architect` |
| Schema, RLS, SQL, migrations | `dba` |
| Coach, LLM, prompts, generated copy | `ai-expert` |
| Implement, fix, refactor | `executor` (plan first via architect/PM if the change is not already specified) |
| Test, QA, smoke, devices | `qa-engineer` |
| Expo, Metro, `.env`, Supabase CLI, GitHub, secrets | `devops` |
| `sync-to-github` | follow that skill (`executor` if you need a subagent) |
| Question, summary, or already-answered | main chat only |

Typical build pipeline (skip steps that do not apply):

`product-manager` → `ui-ux-designer` and/or `software-architect` → `dba` and/or `ai-expert` → `executor` → `qa-engineer`

## Do not

- Launch all seven on every message
- Re-open product debates inside `executor`
- Print secrets
- Skip the **Agents:** line
